#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef650886-8d46-583e-bad0-1429ba496479" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "61ebe3c8-1241-59f1-9d60-704d520c53fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-13055" :question/problem "Which of the following is a variable?\n\nI. $x$\n\nII. $x+1$\n\nIII. $1$\n\nIV. $x+1=2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each one in turn.\n\nI. $x$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n\nII. $x+1$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n\nIII. $1$ is a number, not a variable.\n\nIV. $x+1=2$ contains an equals sign $(=)$ and is an **equation**, not a variable. You'll learn more about equations later.\n\nSo, only choice I represents a variable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae662093-c3e8-5577-af6e-7e2f383da79d" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Between Phrases and Algebraic Expressions Containing Addition"}] :question/id #uuid "ee12fc6a-91b2-5855-96a8-c28bd6652ae5" :question/math-academy-id "e-13056" :question/problem "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The sum of three and a number.\"" :question/worked-solution "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the sum of three and a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\n3+x.\n$$\n\n**Note:** There are other correct answers as well. We could choose another letter, such as $a$, to represent the number. In that case, \"the sum of three and a number\" could also be written as \n\n$$\n3+a.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054423 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fc32821-14d0-5cbe-b8d9-4e7ff5cc937b" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Between Phrases and Algebraic Expressions Containing Subtraction"}] :question/id #uuid "ebd7ac34-c0e4-5e42-940a-cce33864a7de" :question/math-academy-id "e-13057" :question/problem "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The difference of eight and a number.\"" :question/worked-solution "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the difference of eight and a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\n8-x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef650886-8d46-583e-bad0-1429ba496479" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065d61d0-5556-5074-9e29-24c4baf0b670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424905} {:answer/id #uuid "51f9364b-46d6-5468-b5a5-51b352fe40cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424919} {:answer/id #uuid "70e0e846-92fa-5774-9854-8e524132c32b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424931} {:answer/id #uuid "82e897f1-3627-5d02-bcae-87e8a72e0f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424935} {:answer/id #uuid "8d835ea2-e300-5950-9eea-6b60022c260b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d835ea2-e300-5950-9eea-6b60022c260b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424936} :answer-field/id #uuid "63fb59fc-4636-5041-9c29-9ac252842e04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b81b7456-a2b2-5074-8d35-61b208d5668